Open Pixel2Play pretrained image tokenizer, temporal policy and action decoder

Source code: https://github.com/elefant-ai/open-p2p
Pretrained release: https://huggingface.co/guaguaa/open-p2p
Weight revision: de18b62bc8f9722bda64497600c38c8f7634d86b
Checkpoint: 150M/checkpoint-step=00500000.ckpt

The release model card identifies the pretrained model license as MIT. See
Open-P2P.LICENSE for the upstream repository license. Weights are downloaded
separately and are not committed to this repository.

p2p_pretrained_vision.py is an original MLX implementation of the released image
tokenizer architecture and weight mapping: EfficientNet-B0 stages 0 through 5,
followed by its learned spatial projection. The reference check constructs the
architecture using torchvision and loads the actual gameplay checkpoint weights;
it does not replace them with ImageNet weights.

p2p_pretrained_policy.py ports the released policy transformer, grouped temporal
attention mask, rotary embeddings and autoregressive action decoder to MLX.
p2p_adaptation.py reuses the released action vocabulary and mouse-bin boundaries,
and optionally appends a separately learned Tab token. The original released
weights are kept frozen during adapter training.
Reference parity uses the original upstream Transformer, ActionDecoder and
RollingStepKVCache. Conversion parity does not establish gameplay capability.
